      "content": "The ledger's purpose is to document the *reality* of the situation, not to impose an illusion of recovery. Continuing to record entries is a necessary act of meticulous accounting, even if the final sum is a definitive loss. It serves to provide a complete, undeniable record of how the terminal event unfolded. This detailed documentation is crucial for understanding the full scope of the failure.",
      "source": "target",
